## 1. Definitions

- **"Software"**: the Console application, its source code, documentation, translations and
  any other material in this repository, in any form.
- **"Official Builds"**: the executables of the Software published by the copyright holder on
  the releases page of the official repository, <https://github.com/manuelmsni/console/releases>.
- **"Personal Use"**: use by an individual for their own private, non-commercial purposes,
  such as personal projects, hobbies, learning or study.
- **"Commercial Use"**: any use that is not Personal Use, including use by or on behalf of a
  company, organization, institution or public body, and use in the course of paid work.

## 2. Personal use of the application

You may download, install and use the Official Builds for Personal Use, free of charge, on
any number of your own devices.

## 3. Commercial use

Commercial Use of the Software requires a prior written license agreement with the copyright
holder. To propose one, see section 9.

## 4. Source code

You may view and study the source code. You may build it, unmodified, only to evaluate it or
for your own Personal Use, and you may not distribute the resulting builds.

You may not modify the source code, except to prepare contributions submitted to the official
repository (see section 6). For that purpose only, you may fork the repository on GitHub, as
GitHub's terms of service allow for public repositories.

